archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2025-10-30T19:18:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-01T19:49:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nreproducable int v4.5.stable.official [876b29033]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6600 (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21025.10016) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.94 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nTool button callables are generally not something I want showing in my autocompletes and such, so I default to marking them private by starting them with `_`. But, the editor is unhappy with this, issuing the `unused_private_class_variable` warning for these - despite that they ARE used, by the very nature of being an `@export_tool_button`.\n\nI would expect no `unused` warnings of any kind from any variable with `@export_tool_button`, as that export should count as \"use\".\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nDeclare a variable like so: \n```gdscript\n@export_tool_button var _test_stuff: Callable = test\n\nfunc test() -> void:\n    print(\"Testing\")\n```\nThe variable has an `unused_private_class_variable` warning, when it should not.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112214/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112214/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}